.TH MU2EDAQ-FILE-REAPER 1 "2026-09-11" "mu2edaq-file-reaper 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-file-reaper \- policy-driven disk cleanup daemon for the Mu2e DAQ
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-file-reaper
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-scan\-interval\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-database\-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-admin\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-workers\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-discovery\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-\-pid\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.br
.B mu2edaq-file-reaper
\fB\-\-check\-config\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B mu2edaq-file-reaper
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.PP
Equivalent invocations:
.BR "python file_reaper.py" ,
.BR "python \-m mu2edaq_file_reaper" .
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq-file-reaper
runs on a Mu2e DAQ node and keeps the configured disk
.I areas
from filling up.  Every
.I scan_interval
seconds it measures the used fraction of each area's filesystem the way
.BR df (1)
does, compares it with the area's
.BR warning ", " critical " and " full
tiers, alarms the DAQ when a tier is reached, builds an ordered queue of
eligible files under the tier's policy, and compresses or deletes those files
until the tier's low-water mark is reached.  Every decision and action is
written to an audit history.
.PP
A web UI (default port 5004) shows areas, queues, history, exclusions,
notifications and API tokens; a REST API under
.B /api/v1
exposes the same functions with bearer tokens; the
.BR mu2edaq-reaper (1)
command line tool talks to that API.  Each instance advertises itself
through
.B mu2edaq-discovery
with its
.I label
so a cluster of reapers can be found from the control room.
.PP
The daemon never exits because of a bad configuration: problems are reported
on the
.B /config
page and in the log, offending areas are dropped, and everything else keeps
running.  It never acts on an area whose usage it cannot measure.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option except
.B \-\-config
defaults to "not given", so the corresponding value from the environment or
the configuration file applies.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
YAML configuration file.  Default
.IR config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml ,
or
.BR $MU2EDAQ_FILE_REAPER_CONFIG .
A file named explicitly must exist; the default may be absent.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
dotenv file read below the real environment.  Default: a
.I .env
next to the configuration file, then
.I ./.env
if present.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " NAME"
Instance label used in discovery and notifications (default: short hostname).
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDR"
Bind address for the web server (default 0.0.0.0).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Web UI and API port (default 5004).
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-port " PORT"
Serve
.B /api/*
on a second listener as well.
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-interval " SECONDS"
Seconds between scans (default 600).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Plan, publish queues and write history, but never modify the filesystem.
Disk usage is simulated from the planned actions so the report shows exactly
which files a live run would have consumed.
.TP
.BI \-\-database\-url " URL"
SQLAlchemy URL (default
.IR sqlite:///./data/file-reaper.db ;
PostgreSQL via
.IR postgresql+psycopg://user:pw@host/db ).
.TP
.BI \-\-admin\-token " TOKEN"
Secret that unlocks the mutating pages of the web UI and lets
.BR mu2edaq-reaper (1)
mint the first API token.  Prefer the environment or the .env file over the
command line.  When empty a one-time bootstrap token is logged at start.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Areas scanned concurrently (default 4).  Areas on the same filesystem still
take turns.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-discovery
Do not advertise through mu2edaq-discovery.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Detach with the double-fork idiom (POSIX only).  The start script sets this.
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " FILE"
Write the daemon PID here.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " FILE"
Rotating log file (size and count from the configuration).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Load and validate the configuration, print every area and issue, and exit
with status 1 when an area was dropped.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION PRECEDENCE
.PP
.RS
command line  >  environment  >  .env file  >  configuration file  >  built-in defaults
.RE
.PP
A value given at a higher layer replaces the same value from a lower layer;
absent values leave the lower layer in place.  The configuration file format
is described in
.BR mu2edaq-file-reaper.conf (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All variables carry the prefix
.BR MU2EDAQ_FILE_REAPER_ .
.TP
.B CONFIG
Configuration file path.
.TP
.B ENV_FILE
dotenv file path.
.TP
.BR LABEL ", " WEB_HOST ", " WEB_PORT ", " API_PORT ", " SCAN_INTERVAL
As the options of the same name.
.TP
.BR DRY_RUN ", " DAEMON ", " VERBOSE ", " OPEN_READ ", " DISCOVERY
Booleans: 1/true/yes/on or 0/false/no/off.  An unparseable value is warned
about and ignored.
.TP
.BR PID_FILE ", " LOG_FILE ", " ADMIN_TOKEN ", " WORKERS ", " DATABASE_URL
As the options of the same name.
.TP
.B SECRET_KEY
Flask session signing key.  Random per process when unset, which logs every
admin session out at restart.
.TP
.BR CRS_PORT_HTTP ", " CRS_STOP_TIMEOUT
Read by the start and stop scripts, not by the daemon.
.SH TIERS AND WATER MARKS
Thresholds are percent of capacity
.BR used .
For a tier with threshold T, high_water h and low_water l:
.PP
.RS
trigger = min(T + h, 100)
.br
stop    = max(T \- l, 0)
.RE
.PP
The tier becomes active when used >= trigger and stays active, acting on
every scan, until used <= stop.  Within one scan only the most severe active
tier acts; when its queue runs out or its stop point is reached the next
lower active tier gets a pass, up to
.I max_passes_per_scan
passes.  A tier whose queue empties while used space is still above T raises a
.B policy_insufficient
alarm.
.SH POLICIES
.TP
.B LRU-Delete
Order by the more recent of atime and mtime, oldest first; delete.
.TP
.B Age-Delete
Order by mtime, oldest first; delete.
.TP
.B LRU-Compress
As LRU-Delete, but compress in place (X becomes X.gz) keeping atime, mtime,
mode and owner.  Compressed files stay eligible for later delete tiers.
.TP
.B Age-Compress
As Age-Delete, but compress.
.PP
Each tier's
.I min_age
applies to its policy's ordering key.
.SH SAFETY
The reaper refuses to manage system roots or any directory less than two
levels deep (unless
.I allow_shallow_root
is set), never follows symlinks, never crosses a filesystem boundary, skips
hard-linked files, files modified within
.I settle_seconds
and files whose mu2edaq-fts status is not COMPLETED or DELETED when an
.I fts_db
gate is configured (an unreadable FTS database makes nothing eligible).
Every action re-opens the parent directory and the file by descriptor and
verifies device, inode, size, mtime and link count against the scan before
acting; any difference is a skip.  Compression writes to a temporary file in
the same directory, verifies it, renames it into place and only then removes
the original.  The reaper's own database and the FTS database are always
protected.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop the daemon gracefully: in-flight actions finish at the next file or
1 MiB chunk, queued notifications are flushed, and the PID file is removed.
A second signal exits immediately.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml
Reference configuration, heavily commented.
.TP
.I config/mu2e-file-reaper-dl-01.yaml
Host configuration for the mu2e-dl-01 data logger.
.TP
.I config/.env.example
Template for the secrets file.
.TP
.I data/file-reaper.db
Default SQLite database (history, tokens, exclusions, area state,
notification log).
.TP
.I logs/mu2edaq-file-reaper.log
Rotating log.
.TP
.I ./file-reaper.pid
PID file written by the start script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean shutdown; 1 when daemonising fails, when
.B \-\-check\-config
reports a dropped area, or when an explicitly named configuration file is
missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a host configuration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq-file-reaper -c config/mu2e-file-reaper-dl-01.yaml --check-config
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run in the foreground in dry-run mode on another port:
.PP
.RS
.nf
MU2EDAQ_FILE_REAPER_ADMIN_TOKEN=secret \\
  python file_reaper.py -c config/mu2edaq-file-reaper.yaml -p 5010 --dry-run -v
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start and stop as the control room does:
.PP
.RS
.nf
./start-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh -c config/mu2e-file-reaper-dl-01.yaml
./stop-mu2edaq-file-reaper.sh
.fi
.RE
